ula  another one is hopeful you might want to  memorize if you don't know this one  already it's the average of the exes and  it's the average of the wise so just  like you would think you're adding the  x-coordinates together and dividing by 2  adding the Y corners together dividing  by 2 so if we do that we get negative 2  plus 6 divided by 2 and 3 plus 9/2 which  we simplify that it's going to be 4 over  2 which is 2 12 or 2 inches  six so now we know that the center of  our circle is at two comma six right  right to up sticks so so far what we  have is X minus 2 squared plus y minus 6  squared right equals the radius squared  okay now to find the radius you can do a  couple different things okay one thing  you can do is you can say well I know  that my center here is at 26 I know that  a point over here on the circle of 69  you could use the distance formula to  find that radius put it in here and then  square it so just a quick reminder the  distance formula is the square root of  x2 minus x1 squared plus y q minus y1  squared you add those together you take  the square root that's all way to do it  another way to do it this way i like is  you just take one of the points let's  just say we take 69 we put six in for x  ok so that's 6 minus 2 squared we put  nine in for y so that's 9y minus 6  squared we can solve for r squared  that's going to be 4 squared which is 16  3 squared which is 9 so you can see that  r squared is actually going to be 25 so  if we put this all back together our  equation of our circle is x minus 2  squared plus y minus 6 squared equals  the radius squared which is 25 and you  got it okay example number to see if you  can do this one on your own the equation  of the circle is given by this equation  here what is the center of the circle so  they're just asking us for the center  but notice that this equation is not in  our standard form of a circle so we're  going to have to put in that standard  form so we can identify the coordinates  